Package: TTPsplines
Title: Tensor-Train P-Splines for Multidimensional Smoothing and GLMs
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Dae-Jin", "Lee", , "daejin.lee@ie.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-9090-0475")),
    person("Rafael", "Ballester-Ripoll", role = "ctb",
           comment = "planned collaborator")
  )
Description: Tensor-Train (TT) compression of multidimensional P-spline
    coefficient arrays for non-additive smooth regression on scattered
    continuous covariates. Retains the classical discrete P-spline penalty
    on the coefficient tensor Theta; TT changes representation and
    optimization only. Supports Gaussian, Poisson, and Bernoulli responses
    via ALS / PIRLS / L-BFGS, a transparent family-aware optimizer='auto'
    default, fixed anisotropic smoothing, and conditional GCV (cGCV).
    Full-tensor / GLAM baselines are available when feasible. Development
    version; the public API may still change.
